{"content-type": "urn:eclecticiq.com:json:3.0", "enrichments": [], "entities": [], "entities_v2": [{"id": "ent_0dafb2e6", "data": {"title": "S3 buckets (payload hosting)", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_404a779d", "data": {"title": "LDAP-based user activity discovery", "type": "attack-pattern"}}, {"id": "ent_d1d0f8d9", "data": {"title": "Greenshot (trojanized)", "type": "tool"}}, {"id": "ent_f77c6904", "data": {"title": "TukTuk", "type": "malware"}}, {"id": "ent_7db3c3a7", "data": {"title": "Antivirus enumeration", "type": "attack-pattern"}}, {"id": "ent_6c10e9e1", "data": {"title": "Cake (trojanized)", "type": "tool"}}, {"id": "ent_78e40622", "data": {"title": "SyncTrayzor (trojanized)", "type": "tool"}}, {"id": "ent_77579fcd", "data": {"title": "Arweave (dead-drop resolver)", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_9af3aea7", "data": {"title": "Supabase", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_838db15e", "data": {"title": "GitHub (C2 transport)", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_d1056fb9", "data": {"title": "Ably (backup C2 channel)", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_a0247ce7", "data": {"title": "Domain reconnaissance", "type": "attack-pattern"}}, {"id": "ent_8ca4d050", "data": {"title": "GitHub Issues (backup C2 channel)", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_87de56e4", "data": {"title": "Dropbox (backup C2 channel)", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_442bb0ec", "data": {"title": "System profiling / host reconnaissance", "type": "attack-pattern"}}, {"id": "ent_201feed8", "data": {"title": "Direct HTTP (backup C2 channel)", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_6c013e6c", "data": {"title": "ClickHouse (primary C2 channel)", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_88a22853", "data": {"title": "DocFX (trojanized)", "type": "tool"}}, {"id": "ent_177229e8", "data": {"title": "C2 (Command and Control)", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "ent_b4df59ff", "data": {"title": "DLL sideloading", "type": "attack-pattern"}}, {"id": "ent_80f40c6f", "data": {"title": "Slack", "type": "infrastructure"}}, {"id": "rep_2a740ecf", "data": {"title": "Shortly after the config update, the malware initiated extensive host and domain reconnaissance, including system profiling, antivirus enumeration, domain checks, and LDAP-based user activity discovery", "type": "report", "description": ".\n\nThe actor then downloaded additional payloads from S3 buckets, ultimately deploying TukTuk malware variants disguised as Greenshot binaries and executed via DLL sideloading. While Expel has previously reported on Greenshot being abused this way, we also observed the same sideloading technique applied to SyncTrayzor, the DocFX document generator, and the Cake build automation system.\n\nThese trojanized payloads established primary C2 channels through SaaS platforms ClickHouse and Supabase, with secondary backup channels capable of leveraging Ably, Dropbox, direct HTTP, or GitHub Issues.\n\nTukTuk can use Arweave as a dead-drop resolver. In this mode, the implant queries the Arweave blockchain for a specific Drive-Id, then retrieves an encrypted configuration blob. That blob contains the credential pool for all supported C2 transports, including ClickHouse, Supabase, Slack, GitHub, Dropbox, and others. The functionality is fully implemented and connected in the loaded code. However, we could not confirm that this capability was used during this intrusion."}}, {"id": "a25506321e78", "data": {"source": "ent_177229e8", "source_type": "infrastructure", "target": "ent_d1056fb9", "target_type": "infrastructure", "key": "uses", "type": "relation"}, "metadata": {"report_id": "rep_2a740ecf"}}, {"id": "5429de4f5223", "data": {"source": "ent_177229e8", "source_type": "infrastructure", "target": "ent_77579fcd", "target_type": "infrastructure", "key": "uses", "type": "relation"}, "metadata": {"report_id": "rep_2a740ecf"}}, {"id": "f65218ffc8c8", "data": {"source": "ent_177229e8", "source_type": "infrastructure", "target": "ent_6c013e6c", "t